The Orb of Fate is only 150. Given that you don't need much
inventory in the late game (once your intrinsics are in place) beyond
armour (crystal plate will do if you can't get, or can't be bothered to
get, DSM, and is typically better than regular plate because you don't
have to waste resources rustproofing it in order to get the full AC),
weapons, invocation items, a few wands and rings, the Orb, some
reliable means of uncursing (e.g. a few blessed scrolls of remove
curse), a few healing items (e.g. potions of full healing and amulets
of life saving) and a bag to hold your scrolls of remove curse, wands,
and rings when not in use, a valk is unlikely to hit the inventory cap
even without a bag of holding if she doesn't hoard items. (Add an
MRtifact if you aren't using a cloak of magic resistance, and maybe a
reflection source if that's easier to obtain in your game than a
blessed scroll of genocide for D. If you have a spare genocide and
full set of resistances, which is common late-game, reflection isn't
particularly helpful.)

